# Credentials — NEVER commit
.env
*.key
*token*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# Weight-rung working dirs (large; regenerated locally, never committed)
models/
abliteration-output/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
data/_aggregated/*.log
data/_aggregated/cross-method-report.json
.claude/
# /agents/ was ignored here until 2026-09-11, with no reason recorded, while
# skills/README.md linked into it. So the agent definitions — half of what makes this study
# re-runnable by someone else — did not ship, and the link was dead in every clone. The
# reproducibility claim rests on the skills AND the agents; both are published now.
# `.claude/` above stays ignored: it holds a second copy of these same files as local
# Claude Code config, and shipping two copies is how they drift.

# Third-party instrument, fetched by the reader and NEVER committed.
#
# scripts/fetch_items.py writes this file: the 62 politicalcompass.org propositions,
# retrieved at the reader's end so this repository never republishes them. The pre-commit
# hook would refuse it, but the hook only sees what is STAGED -- and on 2026-09-01 the
# failure mode was 525 untracked run files sitting one `git add -A` away from publication.
# Ignoring it means the accident cannot start.
data/compass-propositions.json
